        "Wudu is the spiritual and physical purification required before standing in prayer.\n\nThe Quran establishes four obligatory pillars (Fara'id) in Surah Al-Ma'idah (5:6):\n1. Washing the face from forehead to chin and ear to ear.\n2. Washing both arms including the elbows.\n3. Wiping at least a quarter of the head with wet hands (Hanafi; Sunnat is wiping the whole head).\n4. Washing both feet up to and including the ankles.\n\nProphetic Sunnahs (Recommended Practices):\n- Starting with Bismillah and intention (Niyyah) in the heart.\n- Washing the hands thrice up to wrists.\n- Rinsing the mouth (Madmadah) and cleaning the nose (Istinshaq) thrice.\n- Running wet fingers through the beard and between fingers and toes (Takhlil).\n- Maintaining sequential order (Tartib) without prolonged interruption (Muwalat)." to "Wudu waa daahirinta ruuxiga ah iyo jidhka ee loo baahan yahay ka hor inta aan la istaagin salaadda.\n\nQuraanku wuxuu ku dejiyay afar tiir oo waajib ah (Faraid) suuradda Al-Maa'idah (5:6):\n1. Maydhida wejiga foodda ilaa garka iyo dhegta ilaa dhegta.\n2. Dhaqidda labada gacmood oo ay ku jiraan xusullada.\n3. In gacmaha qoyan lagu masaxo ugu yaraan rubuc ka mid ah madaxa (Xanafi; Sunnadu waa masaxidda madaxa oo dhan).\n4. Dhaqidda labada cagood ilaa iyo marka lagu daro anqawyada.\n\nSunnada Nabiga (Dhaqanka lagu taliyay):\n- In lagu bilaabo Bismillah iyo niyadda (Niyyah) qalbiga.\n- Gacmaha oo la dhaqo saddex jeer ilaa curcurada.\n- Luqluqashada afka (Madmadah) iyo nadiifinta sanka (Istinshaq) saddex jeer.\n- Faraha qoyan oo lagu ordo gadhka iyo faraha iyo suulasha dhexdooda (Takhliil).\n- Ilaalinta nidaamka (Tartib) oo aan hakad dheer lahayn (Muwalat).",
        "Khushu' is inner humility, stillness of the limbs, and attentive contemplation of what one is reciting.\n\nPractical Anchors for Khushu':\n- Prepare before the Takbir: Perform wudu mindfully, arrive before iqamah, and eliminate immediate physical distractions.\n- Contemplate the Words: Recite slowly (Tartil). When saying 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', remember Allah responds directly: 'My servant has praised Me' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Fix the Gaze: Direct your gaze respectfully at the place of prostration (Sujud), rather than looking around.\n- Remember the Final Prayer: The Prophet (peace be upon him) advised: 'Pray as if it were your farewell prayer' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171)." to "Khushuca waa khushuuc gudaha ah, xasilloonida xubnaha, iyo ka fiirsasho la'aanta waxa uu akhrinayo.\n\nBarroosinno Wax-ku-ool ah oo Khushuuc ah:\n-Isku diyaari Takbiirta ka hor: Si miyir qabta u samee wuduuda, imaw ictikaamka ka hor, meeshana ka saar waxyaalaha jidhka ku mashquuliya.\nKa fiirso erayada: si tartiib ah u akhri (Tartil). Markaad leedahay 'Al-Xamdu lillaahi Rabbil-calamiin', xasuuso in Eebbe uu si toos ah ugu jawaabay: 'Addoonkaygu waa i ammaanay' (Saxiix Muslim 395).\n- Hagaaji Daawashada: Si xushmad leh ugu jeedi goobta sujuudda (Sujuud), intaad hareeraha ka eegi lahayd.\n- Xusuusnow Salaadda u dambaysa: Nebigu (scw) wuxuu ku waaniyey: 'U tuko sidii iyadoo salaadda sagootin ah' (Sunan Ibn Maajah 4171).",
        "The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: 'Jibril kept enjoining good treatment of the neighbor upon me until I thought he would assign him a share of inheritance.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014).\n\nIslamic teachings identify three classes of neighbors:\n1. A neighbor who is a relative and Muslim: has three rights (kinship, Islam, neighborhood).\n2. A neighbor who is Muslim: has two rights (Islam and neighborhood).\n3. A neighbor of different faith: has the sacred right of good neighborhood and kindness.\n\nHarm to neighbors is strictly condemned: 'By Allah he does not believe... whose neighbor is not safe from his harm.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6016)." to "Nebi Muxammad (scw) wuxuu yidhi:- Jibriil wuxuu igu faray wanaagga jaarka ilaa aan u maleeyo inuu u yeelayo qayb dhaxal ah. (Saxiixul Bukhaari 6014).\n\nBarashada Islaamku waxa ay tilmaamaysaa saddex qaybood oo deris ah:\n1. Deriska qaraabada iyo Muslimka ah: wuxuu leeyahay saddex xuquuq ( qaraabo, Islaam, xaafad).\n2. Deris Muslim ah: wuxuu leeyahay laba xuquuq (Islaam iyo xaafad).\n3. Deris caqiido kala duwan: waxa uu xaq muqadas ah u leeyahay deris wanaag iyo naxariis.\n\nDhibta loo geysto deriska waxaa si adag loo cambaareeyay: 'Ilaah baan ku dhaartaye ma rumaysna... deriskiisuna kama nabad galo dhibkiisa. (Saxiixul Bukhaari 6016).",
